  "solution": {
    "text": "<br />$\\begin{aligned} & T \\cdot E=K \\cdot E+P . E \\\\ & \\Rightarrow K \\cdot E=T \\cdot E-K \\cdot E \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{2} k^2-\\frac{1}{2} k^2 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow K E=\\frac{1}{2} m \\omega^2\\left(A^2-x^2\\right) \\quad\\left[\\because k=m \\omega^2\\right]\\end{aligned}$<br />$\\mathrm{KE}$ is maximum at $\\mathrm{x}=0$ \\& $\\mathrm{KE}$ is zero when $\\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{A}$ $\\therefore \\mathrm{K} . \\mathrm{E}$ vs $\\mathrm{x}$ graph is parabola.",
